{"id":123011205962800,"type":"artist","name":"Heavenly","artist":null,"year":1989,"weight":17,"info":{"tags":["Power metal","twee","indie pop","symphonic metal","metal"],"country":"GB","begin":"1989","end":"1996","kind":"Group","similar":["Talulah Gosh","Tiger Trap","Dressy Bessy","Gaze","Cub","The Softies","Plumtree","Dark Moor","The Field Mice","Dionysus"],"disambiguation":"British indie group","img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Heanly_point_ephemere_mai_2024.jpg?width=500","bio":"Hay  dos grupos con el nombre Heavenly:\n\n1- Heavenly es un grupo de música pop formado en Oxford en 1989 por tres ex componentes de Talulah Gosh: Amelia Fletcher, Mathew Fletcher y Peter Momtchiloff. A estos se unirían Cathy Rogers, Robert Pursey y Dick Edwards. Fueron los pioneros del movimiento Twee\n\n\n2- Heavenly es un grupo de power metal formado en París por Benjamin Sotto ( vocalista ) y el bajista Max Pirlo en  1994. Sus letras hablan sobre las batallas del bien y el mal , y la vida."},"works":[{"id":254145224803443,"type":"song","name":"I Fell in Love Last Night","artist":"Heavenly","year":1990,"weight":7,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[{"name":"The Ongoing History of New Music","n":2}],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":114476986102119,"type":"album","name":"Heavenly vs. Satan","artist":"Heavenly","year":1991,"weight":15,"yt":"VQKnHmJrUkY","src":"books,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":154989059241510,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — C86","rank":3,"scaruffi":null},{"id":161051722508702,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jangle Pop","rank":99,"scaruffi":null},{"id":198686658475555,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Cuddlecore","rank":2,"scaruffi":null},{"id":251973115798518,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Twee Pop","rank":28,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":4}},{"id":194659899121552,"type":"album","name":"Le Jardin De Heavenly","artist":"Heavenly","year":1992,"weight":