a de la década», cuyo OK Computer es una obra maestra del falso vanguardismo; Coldplay, Travis.","color":"#f472b6","family":"Pop, power-pop y synth-pop","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":114476986102119,"artist":"Heavenly","artist_id":123011205962800,"title":"Heavenly Vs Satan","year":1991,"ess":0,"yt":"tsuxZdb6I9s","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Brit-pop y post-pop","scene_id":193634530822272,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop","chapters":["Sección 6.11"],"pages":[[1,270,null]]},{"id":194659899121552,"artist":"Heavenly","artist_id":123011205962800,"title":"Le Jardin De Heavenly","year":1992,"ess":0,"yt":"mfVcYwSZVTs","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Brit-pop y post-pop","scene_id":193634530822272,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop","chapters":["Sección 6.11"],"pages":[[1,270,null]]},{"id":9386760234501,"artist":"Heavenly","artist_id":123011205962800,"title":"Decline And Fall","year":1994,"ess":0,"yt":"CRAW_-_DkX4","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Brit-pop y post-pop","scene_id":193634530822272,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop","chapters":["Sección 6.11"],"pages":[[1,270,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":270,"text":"…in sculpting memorable and unassuming melodies. Teenage Fanclub produced one of the best imitations of Big Star with Bandwagonesque (1991). Heavenly (2) inherited the Primitives' passion for melodious simplicity. Fronted by former Talulah Gosh's singer Amelia Fletcher, they resurrected the age of…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Father of Heavenly Hiraani Tiger Lily Hutchence","body":"Michael Hutchence of INXS had a daughter named Heavenly Hiraani Tiger Lily with British TV host Paula Yates. \"They had a daughter named Heavenly, Heranny Tiger Lily.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Michael Hutchence","from_id":135259033143151,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Star Kids ｜ From the Archives","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U40hOYy_94E"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Fatherhood and Custody Strain","body":"He became a father to Heavenly Hiraani Tiger Lily with Paula Yates. Despite his pride in fatherhood, he was caught in the midst of the contentious custody battle between Yates and Bob Geldof, a strain that worsened his addictions and existing predilections. \"Michael and Paula were the parents of a baby girl named Heveli, Herani, Tiger Lily. And while he was proud to be a father, Michael was caught in the middle of everything between Paula and Bob.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Michael Hutchins","from_id":127014254836151,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Michael Hutchence: 25 Years Later","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=23OgreyK66o"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Mother of Heavenly Hiraani Tiger Lily Hutchence","body":"She and Michael Hutchence had a daughter named Heavenly Hiraani Tiger Lily. \"They had a daughter named Heavenly, Heranny Tiger Lily.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Paula Yates","from_id":11636144673450,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Star Kids ｜ From the Archives","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U40hOYy_94E"}]}],"charts":[{"id":114476986102119,"type":"album","name":"Heavenly vs. Satan","list_id":154989059241510,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — C86","src":"musthear","rank":3,"year":1991,"note":null,"yt":"VQKnHmJrUkY","scaruffi":null},{"id":114476986102119,"type"